<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cambrai</h1><p class="st-meta">470 CE – 509 CE (approx.) · capital Cambrai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Frankish kingdom around Cambrai, ruled by Clovis' kinsman Ragnachar until Clovis eliminated him.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-cambrai">Cambrai</a> was taken by the Salian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodio">Chlodio</a> in the mid 5th century, and by the 480s it was the seat of a separate Frankish king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragnachar">Ragnachar</a>, a relative of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a>. Known almost only from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragnachar">Ragnachar</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syagrius">Syagrius</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/domain-of-soissons">Domain of Soissons</a> in 486. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory</a> portrays him as a debauched ruler who lost the loyalty of his warriors.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 509 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> bribed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragnachar">Ragnachar's</a> followers with armlets of gilded bronze passed off as gold, defeated him and killed him and his brother Richar with his own axe. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-cambrai">Cambrai</a> was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 470 CE – 509 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:69.05%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>470 CE – 509 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cambrai</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ragnachar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Frankish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=490&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cambrai" aria-label="Kingdom of Cambrai on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4754 433 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Cambrai lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5074 689L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5074 689h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5074 689h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cambrai. <a href="/atlas?year=490&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cambrai">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

